+		// Dropping the word and letting pos run on was the first attempt,
+		// and it only moved the symptom: pos reached 352828 against a
+		// 4416-word region - eighty times past the end and still climbing -
+		// so after about 100 ms of a take nothing was written at all.
+		//
+		// Nothing ever ended the transfer, which is the single fault under
+		// both the 100 ms repeat heard from an assigned pad and the take
+		// that stops carrying audio. Real hardware stops the DMA when the
+		// programmed region is full; do that, and leave pos resting exactly
+		// at the region size so the firmware's own position poll concludes
+		// the take instead of waiting for a counter that never settles.
+		m_dma_timer->adjust(attotime::never);
+		m_drq_handler(CLEAR_LINE);
+		return;
+	}
